BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford BeWell / Stanford Healthy Living] The Science of Your In
 ternal Clock
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T130000
DTSTAMP:20260731T151955Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52901301477030-52901301478057@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Each of us has a natural biological rhythm\, known as a chrono
 type\, that influences when we feel alert\, when we feel sleepy\, and when
  we do our best thinking. Trying to force ourselves into a lifestyle that 
 is out of alignment with our chronotype can contribute to stress\, sleep i
 ssues\, and low productivity.\n\nIn this engaging\, evidence-based webinar
 \, we will explore the four common chronotypes\, also known as the Lion\, 
 Bear\, Wolf\, and Dolphin\, and what they reveal about our daily energy pa
 tterns. Y\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://healthyliving.stanford.edu/cl
 asses/register/class_detail.php?t=1cce34dfd3cbss383d348a508b1be48cc821&ci=
 1252749\nLast synced: 2026-07-31 08:19 PDT
URL:https://healthyliving.stanford.edu/classes/register/class_detail.php?t
 =1cce34dfd3cbss383d348a508b1be48cc821&ci=1252749
END:VEVENT
